2
00:00:53.893 --> 00:00:55.935
You said you knew where she was going.

3
00:00:55.936 --> 00:00:59.439
- I did. She got away.
- From you.

4
00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.983
She was helped
by one of her Mechanical friends.

5
00:01:01.984 --> 00:01:04.526
I chased them.
but they got down here first

6
00:01:04.527 --> 00:01:06.989
and disappeared
before I could get a chair.

7
00:01:08.949 --> 00:01:10.743
You already knew I was down here.

8
00:01:12.411 --> 00:01:15.414
People take notice
of where you go. Robert.

9
00:01:16.123 --> 00:01:18.250
You know what?
I'll-I'll take it from here.

10
00:01:18.918 --> 00:01:21.127
I know Greasetown. And it's still on edge.

11
00:01:21.128 --> 00:01:23.129
I've got Jo and Chad.
I think I can manage.

12
00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.673
I should be here for you.

13
00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:27.802
- We could split up.
- Go home to Anthony.

14
00:01:29.804 --> 00:01:31.097
Spend time with him.

15
00:01:32.181 --> 00:01:34.057
It doesn't have to come to that.

16
00:01:34.058 --> 00:01:36.143
It will if I can't find her.

17
00:01:43.484 --> 00:01:46.152
Camille Sims for Emerson.
I'm below the gap.

18
00:01:46.153 --> 00:01:47.946
When Nichols was a fugitive.
she was caught down here.

19
00:01:47.947 --> 00:01:49.072
Find out where.

20
00:01:49.073 --> 00:01:50.825
Oh. and Judge Sims is headed up.

21
00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:52.827
Keep eyes on him...

22
00:01:53.494 --> 00:01:55.579
- for his safety.
<i>- Copy that</i>.

23
00:02:01.752 --> 00:02:04.505
I need to lie down.

24
00:02:05.923 --> 00:02:07.883
Have some water.

25
00:02:08.466 --> 00:02:12.346
The actual fuck? You're alive?

26
00:02:13.097 --> 00:02:14.348
He's alive?

27
00:02:20.938 --> 00:02:22.189
Here.

28
00:02:24.191 --> 00:02:26.026
Anybody else coming back from the dead?

29
00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:28.070
The old sheriff. maybe his wife?

30
00:02:29.029 --> 00:02:30.364
Did anybody see you?

31
00:02:31.699 --> 00:02:33.199
Just Teddy.

32
00:02:35.536 --> 00:02:36.787
Mr. Kyle.

33
00:02:37.746 --> 00:02:38.831
Mr. Holland.

34
00:02:39.665 --> 00:02:43.252
I'm very glad you're still alive.

35
00:02:47.923 --> 00:02:50.675
I didn't think you'd survive the move.

36
00:02:50.676 --> 00:02:54.846
Isn't there a small part of you
that's happy to see me again?

37
00:03:00.895 --> 00:03:04.774
I remember.
I know what we have to do.

38
00:03:08.986 --> 00:03:10.529
<i>Emerson for Camille Sims</i>.

39
00:03:11.781 --> 00:03:13.698
- Go.
- The address you were looking for

40
00:03:13.699 --> 00:03:17.620
is a workshop on 144.
occupied by Martha Walker.

41
00:03:23.042 --> 00:03:24.460
One of the lines must have been a pipe.

42
00:03:26.295 --> 00:03:27.378
What?

43
00:03:27.379 --> 00:03:31.966
Mr. Kyle put the hard drive I smashed
back together.

44
00:03:31.967 --> 00:03:34.427
The-The diagram you found

45
00:03:34.428 --> 00:03:38.139
showed lines coming in from outside.

46
00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:42.060
There are two lines. One goes to IT.
and the other goes to Judicial.

47
00:03:42.061 --> 00:03:43.645
And I didn't know what the lines were.

48
00:03:43.646 --> 00:03:45.396
but that's why I went to the mines.

49
00:03:45.397 --> 00:03:46.606
Yeah. well. you're an idiot.

50
00:03:46.607 --> 00:03:49.901
They're not gonna put some killer pipe
where criminals dig all day.

51
00:03:49.902 --> 00:03:52.946
There are tunnels in the mines
that go up and down the Silo.

52
00:03:52.947 --> 00:03:55.281
And I almost made it
to the line that goes into IT

53
00:03:55.282 --> 00:03:56.616
when they gassed the mines.

54
00:03:56.617 --> 00:04:01.914
The lines going into IT
carry electricity from Silo 1.

55
00:04:02.414 --> 00:04:07.001
So if the generator stops
there's always power in IT.

56
00:04:07.002 --> 00:04:12.298
So. then the line that goes to Judicial.
th-that's the Safeguard.

57
00:04:12.299 --> 00:04:14.426
I think that's what he said. That's...

58
00:04:14.427 --> 00:04:16.469
- I think that's what Jimmy said.
- Now hold on. who is Jimmy?

59
00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:18.471
Jimmy is the guy that I was with in 17.

60
00:04:18.472 --> 00:04:20.140
That's what... I think that's what he said.

61
00:04:20.141 --> 00:04:25.813
Did this Jimmy tell you
where the lines entered into Judicial?

62
00:04:29.024 --> 00:04:31.152
<i>He had an old blueprint. but...</i>

63
00:04:36.699 --> 00:04:39.869
No. It... I can't... It's gone.

64
00:04:54.258 --> 00:04:55.842
Where's our blueprint?

65
00:04:55.843 --> 00:04:58.553
Look. if we have a blueprint.
it would be on that hard drive

66
00:04:58.554 --> 00:04:59.721
which is back in IT.

67
00:04:59.722 --> 00:05:01.389
We're not gonna get to that.

68
00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:04.476
Well. maybe your new pal. Sims.
can help us find it.

69
00:05:04.477 --> 00:05:05.727
Where is Sims?

70
00:05:05.728 --> 00:05:07.020
He went to head off Camille.

71
00:05:07.021 --> 00:05:10.148
Wait. Is 17 the same as our silo?

72
00:05:10.149 --> 00:05:11.816
Yeah. they're exactly the same.

73
00:05:11.817 --> 00:05:15.361
So. then if we find the pipe in 17.
we find it here.

74
00:05:15.362 --> 00:05:17.655
Is there a way to communicate with Jimmy?

75
00:05:17.656 --> 00:05:20.617
Every silo has its own frequency.
so I can try to...

76
00:05:20.618 --> 00:05:24.371
I never saw him with a radio.
I never found a radio. I...

77
00:05:24.997 --> 00:05:26.831
Camille Sims is coming this way.

78
00:05:26.832 --> 00:05:27.916
Oh. shit.

79
00:05:27.917 --> 00:05:30.085
We're gonna have to move you again.

80
00:05:31.212 --> 00:05:33.088
- Go.
- Shit.

81
00:05:34.882 --> 00:05:36.175
You serious?

82
00:05:37.176 --> 00:05:38.635
How long do we have?

83
00:05:38.636 --> 00:05:40.678
McLain said
when she became Head of Supply

84
00:05:40.679 --> 00:05:43.598
we had 70 years of light bulbs left.

85
00:05:43.599 --> 00:05:46.727
Since someone started stealing them.
it's down to two.

86
00:05:50.481 --> 00:05:51.732
What do we do?

87
00:05:53.734 --> 00:05:56.402
First. we keep this to ourselves.

88
00:05:56.403 --> 00:05:58.363
It's only been three months
since one rebellion.

89
00:05:58.364 --> 00:05:59.573
we can't have another one.

90
00:06:00.908 --> 00:06:03.160
Then we find out who killed Orla Kent.

91
00:06:03.828 --> 00:06:07.080
When we do. we might find out
who stole the light bulbs.

92
00:06:07.081 --> 00:06:09.916
Or if we find out who's
been stealing light bulbs.

93
00:06:09.917 --> 00:06:11.961
maybe we find out who killed Orla Kent.

94
00:06:38.571 --> 00:06:40.239
Before you arrest me. we should talk.

95
00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:42.658
Somewhere with no cameras.

96
00:06:45.161 --> 00:06:48.080
I remember everything.

97
00:08:49.827 --> 00:08:51.786
- Oh. fuck.
- Fuck what?

98
00:08:51.787 --> 00:08:53.288
We're now going 70.

99
00:08:53.289 --> 00:08:55.748
We probably should have tried to jump out
when we were still in the city.

100
00:08:55.749 --> 00:08:58.960
I said that. and then you said
that we would die even at 40.

101
00:08:58.961 --> 00:09:00.462
Only horribly injured.

102
00:09:00.463 --> 00:09:03.006
But now. we'd definitely just be a smear.

103
00:09:03.007 --> 00:09:05.717
Can you just... Can you just try
taking out the key? Please.

104
00:09:05.718 --> 00:09:06.719
No.

105
00:09:12.099 --> 00:09:14.350
- Hey. What?
- If we get the fob away from the van.

106
00:09:14.351 --> 00:09:17.103
- won't it just stop working?
- I hope not.

107
00:09:17.104 --> 00:09:19.732
Your kid tosses it.
and you shut down in the middle of I-95?

108
00:09:20.232 --> 00:09:21.316
Not safe.

109
00:09:21.317 --> 00:09:24.277
Safe is not what
I'm fucking feeling right now.

110
00:09:24.278 --> 00:09:26.321
No brakes. No steering.

111
00:09:26.322 --> 00:09:28.615
This is like what
happened to Charlotte's squadron.

112
00:09:28.616 --> 00:09:30.533
You think someone in Iran is driving this?

113
00:09:30.534 --> 00:09:31.827
I don't know. but someone is.

114
00:09:33.245 --> 00:09:37.207
Stensen's been sounding the alarm
on how AI can be used by hackers. right?

115
00:09:37.208 --> 00:09:38.625
So maybe he was on the <i>Nimitz</i>

116
00:09:38.626 --> 00:09:41.212
because he feared
the planes would be compromised.

117
00:09:41.754 --> 00:09:43.005
And they were.

118
00:09:44.507 --> 00:09:45.716
Too crazy?

119
00:09:47.093 --> 00:09:48.843
I think we're neck-deep in crazy.

120
00:09:52.515 --> 00:09:54.850
I need something with a flat edge.

121
00:10:03.317 --> 00:10:04.318
Damn it.

122
00:10:14.495 --> 00:10:15.538
Uh.

123
00:10:16.622 --> 00:10:17.623
Here.

124
00:10:33.472 --> 00:10:35.307
Do you actually know what you're doing?

125
00:10:35.850 --> 00:10:38.144
Uh. roughly. Brakes are simple.

126
00:10:38.644 --> 00:10:44.232
You step on a pedal. it activates a line
which makes the brake pads squeeze.

127
00:10:44.233 --> 00:10:46.109
But whoever's... driving this.

128
00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:48.611
is doing something
with the electronics to stop that.

129
00:10:48.612 --> 00:10:50.363
So. if I can access the...

130
00:10:50.364 --> 00:10:51.449
- What?
- Fuck!

131
00:10:54.118 --> 00:10:55.285
Damn it.

132
00:10:55.286 --> 00:10:56.537
Oh.

133
00:11:01.041 --> 00:11:02.042
Let me see.

134
00:11:14.013 --> 00:11:15.222
Think you'll live?

135
00:11:16.056 --> 00:11:17.057
Sure hope so.

136
00:11:24.774 --> 00:11:26.108
I know about the voice.

137
00:11:27.693 --> 00:11:29.320
- What voice?
- No. don't do that.

138
00:11:30.905 --> 00:11:32.740
I'm not gonna talk to you about this.

139
00:11:33.991 --> 00:11:36.577
Camille. you know I didn't go
into a refuge hut.

140
00:11:37.203 --> 00:11:41.332
I don't know what it tells you.
but I went into another silo.

141
00:11:42.583 --> 00:11:43.917
Hmm.

142
00:11:43.918 --> 00:11:46.670
It's not dead. There are kids in it.

143
00:11:47.213 --> 00:11:49.881
And they're alone. and somehow
they've managed to survive.

144
00:11:49.882 --> 00:11:52.258
But I promised them
that I would go back to them.

145
00:11:52.259 --> 00:11:53.885
That's what I remember.

146
00:11:53.886 --> 00:11:56.471
I remember that I said
I would bring them back here.

147
00:11:56.472 --> 00:12:00.642
- That's an insane request.
- Let me ask the voice. and it can decide.

148
00:12:00.643 --> 00:12:01.685
No.

149
00:12:04.855 --> 00:12:07.066
You know people treat me
like a living Founder.

150
00:12:07.691 --> 00:12:09.485
If I jump off the stairs. they'll follow.

151
00:12:10.986 --> 00:12:12.738
You wanna see what else
they're willing to do for me?

152
00:12:13.405 --> 00:12:15.657
You sound like a threat to the Silo.

153
00:12:15.658 --> 00:12:20.371
No. Camille. I want to save the kids.

154
00:12:28.087 --> 00:12:31.006
You sure there are no cameras here?
It looks like it knows we're talking.

155
00:12:44.311 --> 00:12:46.230
- Any luck?
- No.

156
00:12:47.314 --> 00:12:49.525
There has to be some way
to stop this thing.

157
00:12:52.153 --> 00:12:53.612
- Oh. oh!
- What?

158
00:12:54.572 --> 00:12:59.117
Hey. hey. hey. hey. hey!
Hey! Stop! Call the police!

159
00:12:59.118 --> 00:13:01.537
Help. help. help. help!
Stop. stop. stop. stop!

160
00:13:02.121 --> 00:13:06.959
Please. please. please!
Call the police! Stop! Hey!

161
00:13:10.087 --> 00:13:11.255
What the fuck?

162
00:13:13.048 --> 00:13:14.300
What happened?

163
00:13:17.636 --> 00:13:19.138
I think I know how to stop this thing.

164
00:13:20.848 --> 00:13:24.100
Hank. I make things. I don't steal them.

165
00:13:24.101 --> 00:13:26.311
We're just hoping
you know somebody who does.

166
00:13:26.312 --> 00:13:29.814
I only associate
with Pact-abiding citizens. you know that.

167
00:13:29.815 --> 00:13:33.610
Mark. we... we've got something
pretty serious going on.

168
00:13:33.611 --> 00:13:35.320
We could really use your help.

169
00:13:35.321 --> 00:13:38.281
Serious. like getting chucked
over the rail?

170
00:13:38.282 --> 00:13:41.659
There are two raiders guilty of throwing
my best friend to his death

171
00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:43.244
during the rebellion.

172
00:13:43.245 --> 00:13:45.455
But I don't hear you asking about that.

173
00:13:45.456 --> 00:13:49.293
This friend of yours.
was his name Lee Torgenson?

174
00:13:50.252 --> 00:13:52.837
And was he thrown over
for using a weapon you made for him?

175
00:13:52.838 --> 00:13:55.549
- Oh. fuck you. Who the fuck are you?
- I'm the sheriff.

176
00:13:56.092 --> 00:13:58.301
- And if you don't cooperate. we...
- You're not a sheriff.

177
00:13:58.302 --> 00:14:00.095
- You're an accident.
- Mark.

178
00:14:00.096 --> 00:14:01.346
You got the job by default.

179
00:14:01.347 --> 00:14:03.765
Now you're standing here
wearing Holston's hand-me-downs.

180
00:14:03.766 --> 00:14:05.683
and they're one size too big.

181
00:14:05.684 --> 00:14:07.018
You wanna arrest someone?

182
00:14:07.019 --> 00:14:08.770
- Arrest your wife.
- Mark!

183
00:14:08.771 --> 00:14:11.147
You think people don't know
about her and the Outsiders?

184
00:14:11.148 --> 00:14:12.941
Trying to get us all killed?

185
00:14:12.942 --> 00:14:15.986
Oh. What are you going to do. Mr. Sheriff?
Drag me out of here?

186
00:14:16.779 --> 00:14:18.030
That'll look great.

187
00:14:21.408 --> 00:14:22.868
Mark. we are not threatening you.

188
00:14:23.494 --> 00:14:25.995
We're just in a tough spot.
and we really need to know

189
00:14:25.996 --> 00:14:29.874
if anyone has info on things
disappearing from Critical Supply.

190
00:14:29.875 --> 00:14:32.378
I'm not doing shit for this asshole.

191
00:14:37.716 --> 00:14:39.135
How about this...

192
00:14:40.302 --> 00:14:44.974
You give us something we can use.
and I'll look into the raiders.

193
00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:47.851
- You won't do anything...
- I'll get their names.

194
00:14:47.852 --> 00:14:51.689
I'll give them to you. Whatever you do
with that information is up to you.

195
00:15:05.035 --> 00:15:06.036
All right.

196
00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:12.585
Here's this...
The weapons I made. I made for Knox.

197
00:15:13.169 --> 00:15:15.004
You wanna know about stolen shit?

198
00:15:16.338 --> 00:15:18.382
His father was crooked as a screw.

199
00:15:19.341 --> 00:15:21.342
He used to steal
diamond drill bits from Supply.

200
00:15:21.343 --> 00:15:23.095
and sold 'em on the black market
as jewelry.

201
00:15:23.846 --> 00:15:25.598
Far as I know. he's out of that game.

202
00:15:26.348 --> 00:15:28.058
But he'll know more than I will.

203
00:15:28.642 --> 00:15:30.186
That something you can use?

204
00:15:36.358 --> 00:15:37.526
Get me those names.

205
00:15:39.445 --> 00:15:41.155
- You all right?
- I'm fine.

206
00:15:52.875 --> 00:15:55.336
We just sit. and we wait.

207
00:15:56.128 --> 00:15:58.046
Come on.
All it takes is one person

208
00:15:58.047 --> 00:16:01.634
to see an empty van driving by itself.
and they will call the cops.

209
00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:07.306
Oh. ye of little faith.

210
00:16:34.041 --> 00:16:37.378
<i>Juliette Nichols. why are you here?</i>

211
00:16:43.759 --> 00:16:44.927
You just speak.

212
00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:47.763
Okay. Um...

213
00:16:49.765 --> 00:16:51.976
I know what happened when I went outside.

214
00:16:52.643 --> 00:16:58.065
And... In Silo 17 there are kids.
and I want to bring them back. Here.

215
00:17:03.112 --> 00:17:05.948
Silo 17 is flooding.
a-and they're gonna die.

216
00:17:10.536 --> 00:17:14.707
I'm not working against the Silo.
I'm not working against you.

217
00:17:15.749 --> 00:17:17.126
I'm not a threat.

218
00:17:22.381 --> 00:17:25.508
<i>The numbers predict
disaster for the Silo if you leave.</i>

219
00:17:25.509 --> 00:17:26.968
<i>Request is denied.</i>

220
00:17:26.969 --> 00:17:29.763
No. not me.
We'll send someone else to get them.

221
00:17:29.764 --> 00:17:31.222
<i>The numbers predict disaster</i>

222
00:17:31.223 --> 00:17:34.226
<i>if residents from another silo
join Silo 18</i>.

223
00:17:35.352 --> 00:17:36.728
<i>Request is denied</i>.

224
00:17:36.729 --> 00:17:40.065
No. but they're kids.
They're gonna die in 17.

225
00:17:41.817 --> 00:17:45.278
<i>They'd be invasive.
Request is denied.</i>

226
00:17:45.279 --> 00:17:47.698
Time to leave. Come on.

227
00:17:54.914 --> 00:17:58.667
Okay. what if I go back on
the memory drug? Is that what you want?

228
00:17:59.794 --> 00:18:01.045
I'll do it.

229
00:18:05.508 --> 00:18:07.760
You can even drug the kids.

230
00:18:10.304 --> 00:18:12.389
And then they won't be a threat
to anyone here. right?

231
00:18:18.562 --> 00:18:19.980
<i>How many children?</i>

232
00:18:28.697 --> 00:18:30.449
I think you're making a play.

233
00:18:31.617 --> 00:18:32.827
- I'm not.
- You're not?

234
00:18:34.286 --> 00:18:37.497
- You have my word.
- I have your word. really?

235
00:18:37.498 --> 00:18:39.458
You lied to me.

236
00:18:40.084 --> 00:18:45.506
You drugged me for three fucking months.
and you question my honesty?

237
00:18:48.717 --> 00:18:52.638
I'll find someone to get the kids.
and then I'll go back to being your mayor.

238
00:19:05.192 --> 00:19:06.193
What?

239
00:19:06.735 --> 00:19:08.654
We're in the middle of fucking nowhere.

240
00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:14.492
Don't rental cars have.
like... locator things?

241
00:19:14.493 --> 00:19:17.579
I got this from Joe's sketchy car rental.
There's no locator.

242
00:19:20.916 --> 00:19:23.501
You're a congressman.
so people are gonna notice

243
00:19:23.502 --> 00:19:24.919
if you don't show up for work.

244
00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:26.713
Not for at least a day.

245
00:19:26.714 --> 00:19:29.759
They'll just be glad I'm not babbling
about infrastructure reform.

246
00:19:30.885 --> 00:19:31.886
What about Charlotte?

247
00:19:34.805 --> 00:19:37.640
Saw her a couple of days ago.
she barely knew who I was.

248
00:19:37.641 --> 00:19:40.143
And Crnkovich asked me
to stay away for a little bit

249
00:19:40.144 --> 00:19:41.854
while she gets focused therapy.

250
00:19:42.938 --> 00:19:44.899
But. he said she is doing better. so...

251
00:19:45.775 --> 00:19:46.776
There's that.

252
00:19:50.946 --> 00:19:54.074
You? Any. uh. potential rescuers
in your corner?

253
00:19:55.910 --> 00:19:57.369
I mean...

254
00:19:58.788 --> 00:20:03.584
I got fired. so... nobody there
is expecting to see me ever again.

255
00:20:05.836 --> 00:20:08.589
And I am a pretty shitty friend.

256
00:20:11.092 --> 00:20:13.260
It takes me weeks to call anyone back.

257
00:20:15.262 --> 00:20:16.263
So. no.

258
00:20:21.644 --> 00:20:23.937
- Hmm.
- Hmm?

259
00:20:23.938 --> 00:20:25.063
- You know...
- What?

260
00:20:25.064 --> 00:20:28.066
If they did just want to kill us.
they've had plenty of opportunities.

261
00:20:28.067 --> 00:20:30.527
They could have driven us
into a bridge abutment

262
00:20:30.528 --> 00:20:32.987
or off a cliff. or into a tree.

263
00:20:32.988 --> 00:20:34.657
But they haven't. which. you know.

264
00:20:35.533 --> 00:20:38.119
leaves the possibility
we could be going someplace nice.

265
00:20:47.837 --> 00:20:49.213
We are so fucked.

266
00:21:07.481 --> 00:21:08.858
Where's Lukas and Kennedy?

267
00:21:10.192 --> 00:21:12.026
Kennedy just wouldn't stop talking.

268
00:21:12.027 --> 00:21:16.823
He needs a rest. so. I found them
an empty single down the hallway.

269
00:21:16.824 --> 00:21:18.533
- Good.
- Where did you go?

270
00:21:18.534 --> 00:21:20.035
I went with Camille.

271
00:21:20.619 --> 00:21:23.747
To the Vault.
I. um... I spoke to it.

272
00:21:25.291 --> 00:21:26.624
What did you say?

273
00:21:26.625 --> 00:21:31.129
I said I wanna send two people to 17.
and bring the kids back here.

274
00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:32.506
And it believed you?

275
00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:34.174
I think so.

276
00:21:34.175 --> 00:21:38.429
- Is it a person. or a machine?
- I don't know. Um.

277
00:21:39.930 --> 00:21:41.307
So who you gonna send?

278
00:21:44.351 --> 00:21:46.394
You know. when I went out
I didn't have a choice.

279
00:21:46.395 --> 00:21:47.980
I had to keep going. Right?

280
00:21:49.106 --> 00:21:53.402
There are... There are hundreds.
There are thousands of bodies out there.

281
00:21:54.195 --> 00:21:57.655
So. whoever we send have
to be able to walk through that.

282
00:21:57.656 --> 00:21:59.241
and not wanna turn back.

283
00:22:00.409 --> 00:22:02.328
If I had the choice.
I don't think I could do it.

284
00:22:03.579 --> 00:22:05.580
So. they better be strong.

285
00:22:05.581 --> 00:22:06.582
Yeah.

286
00:22:07.082 --> 00:22:08.333
And they've gotta be smart.

287
00:22:08.334 --> 00:22:11.212
They've gotta find that pipe.
They've gotta figure out how to cap it.

288
00:22:12.004 --> 00:22:14.131
They need to be engineers.

289
00:22:15.716 --> 00:22:17.301
The best you have.

290
00:22:25.142 --> 00:22:26.477
Ask.

291
00:22:27.061 --> 00:22:28.938
They can always say no.

292
00:22:38.280 --> 00:22:40.199
Shirl. what's going on?

293
00:22:40.825 --> 00:22:42.535
- Why don't you sit down?
- No. it's...

294
00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:52.920
I can't stop thinking
all of us could be gone.

295
00:22:55.673 --> 00:22:58.425
Before we ever get a chance to...

296
00:22:58.426 --> 00:22:59.427
I know.

297
00:23:00.469 --> 00:23:02.304
But we can't think like that.

298
00:23:04.765 --> 00:23:07.267
We just have to focus on...

299
00:23:07.268 --> 00:23:08.602
on what we can do.

300
00:23:22.366 --> 00:23:23.659
Knox.

301
00:23:25.828 --> 00:23:27.288
I need a word with you.

302
00:23:32.585 --> 00:23:33.668
About what?

303
00:23:33.669 --> 00:23:34.879
Your father.

304
00:23:38.549 --> 00:23:39.966
This is not a good time.

305
00:23:39.967 --> 00:23:41.301
Yeah. it'll just take a minute.

306
00:23:41.302 --> 00:23:43.928
What do you know about his connection
to the market in stolen goods?

307
00:23:43.929 --> 00:23:45.346
I'm not doing this right now.

308
00:23:45.347 --> 00:23:46.806
- Why not?
- 'Cause I'm not.

309
00:23:46.807 --> 00:23:48.183
Are you trying to protect him?

310
00:23:48.184 --> 00:23:50.477
Are you fucking kidding me?
Are you really asking me that?

311
00:23:50.478 --> 00:23:52.646
- Yes. I am because if you are...
- What?

312
00:23:54.440 --> 00:23:55.816
What are you gonna do?

313
00:23:57.860 --> 00:23:59.819
- You think that badge means shit to me?
- Hank.

314
00:23:59.820 --> 00:24:02.155
All right. Just-Just calm down.

315
00:24:02.156 --> 00:24:03.199
All right?

316
00:24:03.699 --> 00:24:05.409
This is about a murder.

317
00:24:06.452 --> 00:24:08.537
- Who?
- Orla Kent.

318
00:24:09.371 --> 00:24:11.498
- I don't know her.
- The hell you don't.

319
00:24:11.499 --> 00:24:14.542
She was the shadow to the head of Supply.
She was at the Silo Council...

320
00:24:14.543 --> 00:24:16.711
If I say I don't her.
then I don't fucking know her.

321
00:24:16.712 --> 00:24:20.340
Like you apparently don't know me.
Get him the fuck out of here. Hank.

322
00:24:20.341 --> 00:24:21.841
- Move. Let me the fuck at...
- No.

323
00:24:21.842 --> 00:24:22.926
Leave it. Just. don't.

324
00:24:22.927 --> 00:24:25.429
Not now. Just. trust me. Not now.

325
00:24:26.138 --> 00:24:27.264
Trust me.

326
00:24:38.567 --> 00:24:41.653
Hey. Look. you told me Harwood
had a run-in with Orla Kent

327
00:24:41.654 --> 00:24:42.779
at the Council meeting.

328
00:24:42.780 --> 00:24:45.532
Right? You said McLain was suspicious

329
00:24:45.533 --> 00:24:47.325
of Harwood's daughter
when she was shadowing her...

330
00:24:47.326 --> 00:24:48.326
- Glenda.
- Yeah.

331
00:24:48.327 --> 00:24:50.412
Already spoke to her.
Got nothing concrete.

332
00:24:55.042 --> 00:24:57.002
But maybe we can track her movements.

333
00:24:58.963 --> 00:25:00.005
And Orla's.

334
00:25:00.506 --> 00:25:01.673
Track them?

335
00:25:01.674 --> 00:25:02.842
H-How?

336
00:25:10.266 --> 00:25:11.349
What do you want?

337
00:25:11.350 --> 00:25:13.143
Where do you watch the cameras?

338
00:25:13.144 --> 00:25:14.437
Nowhere.

339
00:25:18.399 --> 00:25:21.193
There was a room on 19.
but they've shut it down.

340
00:25:21.819 --> 00:25:24.947
I've been rewriting the Pact.
and I know nothing's changed.

341
00:25:28.451 --> 00:25:29.577
Take us.

342
00:25:32.705 --> 00:25:33.914
What is that?

343
00:25:35.291 --> 00:25:39.920
There was a relic I kept in my pocket for...

344
00:25:40.629 --> 00:25:42.547
years.

345
00:25:42.548 --> 00:25:49.388
Records said that it was found
in a pillowcase a long time ago.

346
00:25:52.057 --> 00:25:54.268
They called such things...

347
00:25:55.394 --> 00:25:58.647
good luck charms.

348
00:25:59.148 --> 00:26:00.608
Well. did it work?

349
00:26:01.776 --> 00:26:07.907
Well. the relic burned
along with some of me. so maybe not.

350
00:26:10.826 --> 00:26:13.036
That said. I'm still alive.

351
00:26:13.037 --> 00:26:17.582
Although. I'm not sure that's good luck.

352
00:26:17.583 --> 00:26:18.876
Oh. boo-hoo.

353
00:26:19.960 --> 00:26:21.753
You're being waited on hand and foot.

354
00:26:21.754 --> 00:26:24.882
All you have to do
is lie back and pontificate.

355
00:26:36.018 --> 00:26:37.895
Why did you keep me alive?

356
00:26:38.646 --> 00:26:42.607
You convinced Sims
not to kill Juliette.

357
00:26:42.608 --> 00:26:43.984
Oh. I know.

358
00:26:45.194 --> 00:26:46.362
It's just...

359
00:26:48.614 --> 00:26:49.989
It can't have been easy.

360
00:26:49.990 --> 00:26:51.075
No.

361
00:26:52.493 --> 00:26:54.494
And you're still a ratshit asshole.

362
00:26:54.495 --> 00:26:56.621
You shouldn't be surprised
if you wake up one morning

363
00:26:56.622 --> 00:26:58.331
with a screwdriver in your neck.

364
00:26:58.332 --> 00:27:01.084
Even as a boy they wanted me dead.

365
00:27:02.545 --> 00:27:04.213
That wasn't a joke.

366
00:27:05.714 --> 00:27:07.675
I was always...

367
00:27:08.426 --> 00:27:11.011
too smart and...

368
00:27:12.304 --> 00:27:14.640
...too quiet.

369
00:27:23.607 --> 00:27:25.233
What's so amusing?

370
00:27:25.234 --> 00:27:27.402
It's just...

371
00:27:27.403 --> 00:27:29.196
It's just something Carla said.

372
00:27:30.406 --> 00:27:33.450
She said if I liked men.
and you liked people.

373
00:27:33.451 --> 00:27:34.910
we'd make a great couple.

374
00:27:37.037 --> 00:27:38.496
That is amusing.

375
00:27:56.932 --> 00:27:58.684
I wanted to apologize.

376
00:27:59.810 --> 00:28:01.061
Now you don't?

377
00:28:06.484 --> 00:28:07.567
It's the wrong tense.

378
00:28:07.568 --> 00:28:10.153
If you actually want to apologize.
it's "I want..."

379
00:28:10.154 --> 00:28:13.072
I want... want to apologize.

380
00:28:13.073 --> 00:28:14.200
Present tense.

381
00:28:15.534 --> 00:28:18.954
For what I said about journalistic fraud.

382
00:28:25.628 --> 00:28:26.629
What happened?

383
00:28:27.963 --> 00:28:29.547
You really didn't look it up?

384
00:28:29.548 --> 00:28:31.801
I just saw there was some thing
at the <i>Post.</i>

385
00:28:32.426 --> 00:28:35.887
"Thing at the <i>Post</i>" makes it sound like
I wore white to a wedding.

386
00:28:35.888 --> 00:28:37.807
I started to read it. and then...

387
00:28:39.934 --> 00:28:41.185
You made something up.

388
00:28:49.443 --> 00:28:54.865
I did a piece on drug addiction
among congressional staffers.

389
00:28:56.242 --> 00:28:58.744
Yeah. Uh. I was careful.

390
00:28:59.995 --> 00:29:01.538
I changed everyone's details

391
00:29:01.539 --> 00:29:04.917
'cause I knew people would try
and read between the lines.

392
00:29:06.085 --> 00:29:07.878
And I wanted to protect my sources.

393
00:29:08.754 --> 00:29:10.172
Protect their anonymity...

394
00:29:11.257 --> 00:29:13.925
but the day it was published.

395
00:29:13.926 --> 00:29:18.681
a quote from a young woman
I called Sharon got everybody talking.

396
00:29:20.558 --> 00:29:21.684
I knew it would.

397
00:29:23.310 --> 00:29:26.605
She implied that drug use
was not limited to staffers.

398
00:29:28.441 --> 00:29:32.194
Rumors... you know. spread
that the Speaker was using.

399
00:29:33.571 --> 00:29:36.490
You can imagine the pressure
to reveal Sharon's identity.

400
00:29:37.533 --> 00:29:41.370
Legislators. prosecutors.
Capitol police. all...

401
00:29:42.329 --> 00:29:45.040
demanding I reveal her real name.

402
00:29:47.626 --> 00:29:50.920
And then those fuck-nuts at
the <i>Washingtonian</i> published a piece saying

403
00:29:50.921 --> 00:29:55.259
Sharon was really Gillian Aikens
who worked in the Speaker's office.

404
00:29:56.343 --> 00:29:57.344
Mm-hmm.

405
00:29:58.846 --> 00:30:00.306
Problem was they were right.

406
00:30:02.558 --> 00:30:03.559
So what did you do?

407
00:30:05.603 --> 00:30:07.021
Only thing I could do.

408
00:30:08.314 --> 00:30:09.814
I published a tearful confession.

409
00:30:09.815 --> 00:30:14.444
said I'd heard some
utterly spurious rumors about the Speaker.

410
00:30:14.445 --> 00:30:16.947
and had made up Sharon.

411
00:30:18.199 --> 00:30:20.493
You gave up your career
to protect a source?

412
00:30:21.076 --> 00:30:23.329
I gave up my career
because I failed Gillian.

413
00:30:26.373 --> 00:30:27.625
If I'd done a better job...

414
00:30:29.418 --> 00:30:31.128
her name would have never come up.

415
00:30:45.059 --> 00:30:47.102
- No.
- Hmm?

416
00:30:47.103 --> 00:30:48.353
What?

417
00:30:48.354 --> 00:30:50.314
You're not going to 17.

418
00:30:51.524 --> 00:30:52.607
I'll go alone.

419
00:30:52.608 --> 00:30:54.484
You can't go alone. No one can.

420
00:30:54.485 --> 00:30:56.779
- Why not?
- In case one of us doesn't make it.

421
00:30:57.488 --> 00:31:00.074
Then... Teddy will come with me.

422
00:31:00.908 --> 00:31:03.285
Jules. could you just give us a second?

423
00:31:05.746 --> 00:31:07.205
I need to make a move.

424
00:31:07.206 --> 00:31:08.707
It won't take long.

425
00:31:17.800 --> 00:31:19.384
I'll tell her.

426
00:31:19.385 --> 00:31:20.760
And if I do that. she'll never let...

427
00:31:20.761 --> 00:31:24.264
You tell her. and I raise this kid alone.

428
00:31:26.183 --> 00:31:30.896
We don't do this. our kid
and everyone in here will never be safe.

429
00:31:32.273 --> 00:31:33.732
Shirl. please.

430
00:31:34.400 --> 00:31:35.943
Let me take someone else.

431
00:31:36.652 --> 00:31:38.611
It's not the same.

432
00:31:38.612 --> 00:31:39.780
You know that.

433
00:31:40.573 --> 00:31:42.533
If you were Jules. who would you send?

434
00:31:44.243 --> 00:31:45.244
Hmm?

435
00:31:45.870 --> 00:31:47.204
Fuck!

436
00:32:11.645 --> 00:32:13.063
It has to be us.

437
00:32:14.398 --> 00:32:15.399
Both of us.

438
00:32:22.198 --> 00:32:23.865
We do this...

439
00:32:23.866 --> 00:32:26.160
and something happens to you.

440
00:32:26.744 --> 00:32:29.997
Something happens...

441
00:32:33.626 --> 00:32:35.503
It's different now. I don't...

442
00:32:38.756 --> 00:32:40.549
I don't know if I'd come back from that.

443
00:32:44.136 --> 00:32:46.304
When we were on our way up
to see the judge.

444
00:32:46.305 --> 00:32:50.101
you said you wanted
to go out to see the distance.

445
00:32:53.729 --> 00:32:55.272
At least we'll see it together.

446
00:33:14.542 --> 00:33:20.004
You have to promise me.
if I go down. you just keep going.

447
00:33:20.005 --> 00:33:21.674
You don't stop. You don't...

448
00:33:22.341 --> 00:33:24.427
You don't try and save me.

449
00:33:28.139 --> 00:33:29.265
You just go.

450
00:33:38.816 --> 00:33:39.900
We'll do it.

451
00:33:42.236 --> 00:33:43.237
Okay.

452
00:34:02.673 --> 00:34:03.758
What's wrong?

453
00:34:07.052 --> 00:34:08.554
You wanna tell her?

454
00:34:14.268 --> 00:34:18.188
Your son stole 12 credits
out of his teacher's desk today.

455
00:34:19.190 --> 00:34:20.608
Another boy saw him.

456
00:34:22.234 --> 00:34:25.905
When confronted by the teacher.
Anthony blamed it on someone else.

457
00:34:27.031 --> 00:34:28.699
Anthony Aaron Sims.

458
00:34:29.867 --> 00:34:31.827
What do you have to say for yourself?

459
00:34:37.500 --> 00:34:39.001
I'm gonna need more than that.

460
00:34:40.753 --> 00:34:43.005
School says if it happens again.

461
00:34:44.005 --> 00:34:47.176
he'll be expelled
and sent to work in Supply.

462
00:34:49.344 --> 00:34:50.596
Anthony. go to your room.

463
00:34:51.597 --> 00:34:52.723
Now!

464
00:35:03.692 --> 00:35:04.777
Supply?

465
00:35:05.402 --> 00:35:06.486
I'm Judge.

466
00:35:06.487 --> 00:35:10.115
You're head of IT.
Doubt if it'll actually happen.

467
00:35:10.116 --> 00:35:11.242
That's your solution?

468
00:35:11.826 --> 00:35:13.743
Use our positions to fix it?

469
00:35:13.744 --> 00:35:15.995
- It's not what I said.
- No.

470
00:35:15.996 --> 00:35:19.457
No. of course not. I have to read
between the lines like always.

471
00:35:19.458 --> 00:35:21.377
Meaning?

472
00:35:27.383 --> 00:35:29.176
You're avoiding the problem.

473
00:35:30.219 --> 00:35:31.678
I went to the school.

474
00:35:31.679 --> 00:35:33.764
I talked to the principal.

475
00:35:34.306 --> 00:35:36.559
I apologized to the teacher.

476
00:35:37.059 --> 00:35:38.435
What am I avoiding?

477
00:35:38.436 --> 00:35:40.353
Don't do that. Don't guilt-trip me.

478
00:35:40.354 --> 00:35:43.274
If you feel guilt. it's not my fault.

479
00:35:43.941 --> 00:35:45.942
Are we still talking about Anthony?

480
00:35:45.943 --> 00:35:47.403
I'm not sure.

481
00:35:48.737 --> 00:35:49.738
Are we?

482
00:35:54.994 --> 00:35:59.457
You need to stop
everything you've been doing.

483
00:36:00.708 --> 00:36:02.251
You've been watchin' me.

484
00:36:04.587 --> 00:36:06.629
You think I can't spot a tail?

485
00:36:06.630 --> 00:36:09.091
You're making me afraid. Rob.

486
00:36:10.426 --> 00:36:11.593
For our son.

487
00:36:11.594 --> 00:36:12.969
For our family.

488
00:36:12.970 --> 00:36:16.974
Because whatever you're hiding.
when I find out what it is...

489
00:36:19.018 --> 00:36:21.228
I'm gonna have to do something about it.

490
00:36:37.244 --> 00:36:39.789
Hmm.

491
00:36:40.873 --> 00:36:43.000
- Hmm?
- You. uh... Um...

492
00:36:45.211 --> 00:36:46.461
Well. you kept the PEZ.

493
00:36:46.462 --> 00:36:48.171
Didn't even know I had it.

494
00:36:48.172 --> 00:36:49.590
- Really?
- Mmm.

495
00:36:50.174 --> 00:36:52.342
- Wasn't a memento?
- No.

496
00:36:52.343 --> 00:36:55.970
Something to help you remember
the world's worst blind date?

497
00:36:55.971 --> 00:36:57.639
- It wasn't a date.
- Oh.

498
00:36:57.640 --> 00:36:58.724
Right.

499
00:37:06.857 --> 00:37:08.066
Shit.

500
00:37:08.067 --> 00:37:09.902
- Oh. my God.
- You were right.

501
00:37:10.653 --> 00:37:12.780
I honestly didn't think we had
a hope in hell.

502
00:37:28.462 --> 00:37:30.130
They're not stopping us.

503
00:37:30.131 --> 00:37:31.549
Because they don't want to.

504
00:37:33.592 --> 00:37:34.885
They're our escort.

505
00:37:51.110 --> 00:37:52.278
I think it's a mistake.

506
00:37:57.032 --> 00:37:58.242
Hello?

507
00:38:02.538 --> 00:38:03.539
You there?

508
00:38:06.584 --> 00:38:08.335
<i>What is a mistake?</i>

509
00:38:11.547 --> 00:38:15.593
Allowing Juliette
to send someone to Silo 17.

510
00:38:16.093 --> 00:38:18.262
She's after more than the children.

511
00:38:21.265 --> 00:38:23.100
If there are any children.

512
00:38:28.481 --> 00:38:29.815
You don't know. do you?

513
00:38:30.691 --> 00:38:34.527
<i>Whether or not there are
children in Silo 17 does not matter</i>.

514
00:38:34.528 --> 00:38:37.865
How? How-How does it not matter?

515
00:38:39.575 --> 00:38:41.786
<i>You're not
really interested in an answer.</i>

516
00:38:42.286 --> 00:38:43.954
<i>You are looking for an argument.</i>

517
00:38:44.622 --> 00:38:46.039
<i>I will not engage.</i>

518
00:38:46.040 --> 00:38:47.457
Fuck off.

519
00:38:47.458 --> 00:38:50.336
<i>Your heart rate
and respiration are elevated.</i>

520
00:38:50.836 --> 00:38:53.046
Okay.

521
00:38:53.047 --> 00:38:56.716
I feel Juliette is a threat to the Silo.

522
00:38:56.717 --> 00:39:00.887
My husband is lying to me.
and my son is a thief.

523
00:39:00.888 --> 00:39:02.138
All of that...

524
00:39:02.139 --> 00:39:04.599
All of that is on me.

525
00:39:04.600 --> 00:39:08.354
As head of IT.
as a wife. as a mother.

526
00:39:09.605 --> 00:39:10.648
And...

527
00:39:14.068 --> 00:39:15.236
I'm failing.

528
00:39:18.697 --> 00:39:19.865
I'm failing.

529
00:39:27.623 --> 00:39:28.624
Fuck.

530
00:39:33.420 --> 00:39:35.464
<i>I'm sorry you feel that way.</i>

531
00:39:37.007 --> 00:39:39.467
<i>but thoughts aren't facts.</i>

532
00:39:39.468 --> 00:39:43.472
<i>That sense of failure is the result
of being emotionally exhausted.</i>

533
00:39:45.433 --> 00:39:49.937
<i>You need to find a moment
for yourself. To reflect.</i>

534
00:39:51.272 --> 00:39:52.273
Yeah.

535
00:40:00.156 --> 00:40:01.490
I don't know how.

536
00:40:04.034 --> 00:40:07.079
<i>You've already started
by acknowledging your negative thoughts.</i>

537
00:40:08.622 --> 00:40:10.916
<i>Your breathing has started to normalize.</i>

538
00:40:13.002 --> 00:40:16.172
<i>You were chosen for a difficult job
because you are capable.</i>

539
00:40:18.591 --> 00:40:21.343
<i>Take time
to remind yourself of that. Camille.</i>

540
00:40:23.471 --> 00:40:25.848
<i>It is not a job just anyone can do.</i>

541
00:40:35.900 --> 00:40:37.026
Thank you.

542
00:40:50.956 --> 00:40:52.457
You're not supposed to be in here.

543
00:40:52.458 --> 00:40:55.085
This place is not in the Pact.
so there is no here.

544
00:40:56.045 --> 00:40:57.046
Out.

545
00:41:02.635 --> 00:41:05.513
Supposed to be
only a few cameras left for security.

546
00:41:06.013 --> 00:41:07.139
Someone lied.

547
00:41:07.640 --> 00:41:08.932
Move.

548
00:41:12.728 --> 00:41:15.814
Orla Kent's body was found
in the mines two days ago.

549
00:41:15.815 --> 00:41:17.232
Right after the gas.

550
00:41:17.233 --> 00:41:19.442
Show me the mines right before that.

551
00:41:19.443 --> 00:41:20.860
There's no cameras in the mines.

552
00:41:20.861 --> 00:41:22.822
I'm sure there's one at the entrance.

553
00:41:28.160 --> 00:41:30.620
Keep going. Further back.

554
00:41:30.621 --> 00:41:33.958
Look. you're gonna see
the extermination team go in.

555
00:41:35.209 --> 00:41:36.918
with the miners inside.

556
00:41:36.919 --> 00:41:38.003
Why?

557
00:41:39.130 --> 00:41:40.922
They were tryna flush out Lukas Kyle.

558
00:41:40.923 --> 00:41:42.424
You gassed the mines?

559
00:41:42.425 --> 00:41:43.925
I was following orders.

560
00:41:43.926 --> 00:41:44.969
Show us.

561
00:41:51.600 --> 00:41:52.684
Wait.

562
00:41:52.685 --> 00:41:53.686
Stop.

563
00:41:54.603 --> 00:41:56.271
No. that's Glenda Harwood.

564
00:41:56.272 --> 00:41:57.648
We need Orla Kent.

565
00:42:05.448 --> 00:42:07.700
Show us the stairs. ten levels down.

566
00:42:11.036 --> 00:42:12.413
See Orla?

567
00:42:15.040 --> 00:42:16.125
Nothing.

568
00:42:23.174 --> 00:42:25.092
Show us Supply at the same time.

569
00:42:30.973 --> 00:42:32.975
No. Wait. Stop. What's...

570
00:42:35.227 --> 00:42:36.270
Is that Glenda?

571
00:42:36.771 --> 00:42:38.980
- Wasn't she just in the mines?
- Is this at the same time?

572
00:42:38.981 --> 00:42:40.774
Yeah. the same ten minutes.

573
00:42:40.775 --> 00:42:43.277
How did Glenda get
from the mines to Supply in ten minutes?

574
00:42:44.612 --> 00:42:45.613
I don't know.

575
00:42:51.118 --> 00:42:52.745
It won't let you send them.

576
00:42:54.038 --> 00:42:55.956
I need to send people
who can get shit done.

577
00:42:56.707 --> 00:42:58.041
That's Knox and that's Shirley.

578
00:42:58.042 --> 00:43:00.543
That's why they can't go.

579
00:43:00.544 --> 00:43:02.712
They're needed here.
Choose someone expendable.

580
00:43:02.713 --> 00:43:05.090
But for the kids
to be able to make it back.

581
00:43:05.091 --> 00:43:07.301
I need to send Knox and Shirley.

582
00:43:07.885 --> 00:43:09.427
It can't be Knox and Shirley.

583
00:43:09.428 --> 00:43:12.013
The voice gave me permission.

584
00:43:12.014 --> 00:43:14.474
That's nice.
but until it grows a pair of arms

585
00:43:14.475 --> 00:43:18.813
and learns how to walk.
I'm the one who opens the door.

586
00:43:19.647 --> 00:43:20.981
Choose someone else.

587
00:43:24.193 --> 00:43:27.571
Okay. Let's send. um. Kennedy and Lukas.

588
00:43:30.407 --> 00:43:31.491
You know where they are?

589
00:43:31.492 --> 00:43:32.575
- Yeah.
- Where?

590
00:43:32.576 --> 00:43:35.454
Well. considering you want them dead.
I'm not gonna tell you.

591
00:43:36.372 --> 00:43:39.917
Considering you want them dead.
you won't mind sending them out.

592
00:44:18.247 --> 00:44:20.541
That thing earlier with Billings?

593
00:44:21.792 --> 00:44:23.043
Kind of intense.

594
00:44:25.004 --> 00:44:27.298
Yeah. he's an asshole.

595
00:44:29.925 --> 00:44:32.303
I meant your reaction
when he mentioned your father.

596
00:44:34.013 --> 00:44:35.598
My father's an asshole too.

597
00:44:41.020 --> 00:44:42.354
So you gonna tell me?

598
00:44:47.276 --> 00:44:48.694
He was never around.

599
00:44:51.280 --> 00:44:53.199
I mean. maybe you'll remember growing up...

600
00:44:54.700 --> 00:44:56.327
it was just me and my mom.

601
00:44:58.829 --> 00:45:01.832
And it was hard. We struggled.

602
00:45:03.417 --> 00:45:04.959
Never enough food.

603
00:45:04.960 --> 00:45:07.671
I never had... clothes that fit.

604
00:45:09.548 --> 00:45:11.925
I remember when I was a little kid.

605
00:45:11.926 --> 00:45:16.931
I wanted one of those.
uh... those Freedom Day lanterns.

606
00:45:17.431 --> 00:45:19.475
I wanted one so bad.

607
00:45:20.351 --> 00:45:21.560
Couldn't afford it.

608
00:45:27.316 --> 00:45:28.734
But we were okay.

609
00:45:31.237 --> 00:45:32.446
'Cause my mom...

610
00:45:34.990 --> 00:45:36.951
she worked her ass off.

611
00:45:39.328 --> 00:45:40.703
Somehow she still...

612
00:45:40.704 --> 00:45:42.706
she still made time for me.

613
00:45:46.127 --> 00:45:48.254
I don't know when she slept.

614
00:45:53.592 --> 00:45:54.969
Where was your dad?

615
00:45:56.345 --> 00:45:57.638
The mines.

616
00:45:59.723 --> 00:46:01.683
He was supposedly a great engineer.

617
00:46:01.684 --> 00:46:05.646
but he was always in trouble
for breaking the Pact.

618
00:46:07.440 --> 00:46:09.859
Trading stolen goods mostly I think.

619
00:46:13.237 --> 00:46:15.906
But the truth is. he just loved that life.

620
00:46:18.784 --> 00:46:20.327
More than he loved us.

621
00:46:22.538 --> 00:46:25.206
Thing is.
him being gone wasn't the problem.

622
00:46:25.207 --> 00:46:27.084
The problem was when he came home.

623
00:46:27.668 --> 00:46:30.296
He'd turn up
after a stint in the mines. full of it.

624
00:46:31.130 --> 00:46:33.716
Always tryna start shit with my mom.

625
00:46:35.176 --> 00:46:37.428
He would fuck our lives up.

626
00:46:40.055 --> 00:46:44.100
Then he'd get arrested.
and be gone again.

627
00:46:44.101 --> 00:46:47.146
And the cycle would repeat.

628
00:46:50.691 --> 00:46:52.651
I haven't seen him in years.

629
00:47:00.618 --> 00:47:01.869
Thanks for telling me.

630
00:47:02.703 --> 00:47:04.371
But. uh...

631
00:47:05.122 --> 00:47:08.584
Now you've gotten it off your chest.
go help Billings.

632
00:47:10.461 --> 00:47:11.879
A girl's been murdered.

633
00:47:14.173 --> 00:47:15.508
You might be able to help.

634
00:47:32.733 --> 00:47:34.026
Thanks for coming. Asa.

635
00:47:34.527 --> 00:47:36.779
I have a choice?

636
00:47:37.363 --> 00:47:40.365
IT has detected low instances
of Vitamin D.

637
00:47:40.366 --> 00:47:42.409
We need to add a boost
to the water supply.

638
00:47:43.619 --> 00:47:45.036
Okay.

639
00:47:45.037 --> 00:47:47.705
You'll need to turn off
the osmosis filtration system

640
00:47:47.706 --> 00:47:49.041
before we add it.

641
00:47:51.001 --> 00:47:52.711
- Uh...
- Is there a problem?

642
00:48:09.186 --> 00:48:10.770
Okay. shit-heels.

643
00:48:10.771 --> 00:48:12.313
Eyes on me.

644
00:48:12.314 --> 00:48:16.444
You're not here because you stole.
or cheated. or broke the Pact.

645
00:48:17.945 --> 00:48:21.907
You're here because you were too stupid
to get away with it.

646
00:48:24.201 --> 00:48:25.327
Word of advice.

647
00:48:26.287 --> 00:48:28.831
Do not try and be stupid in here

648
00:48:29.540 --> 00:48:30.874
because if you do.

649
00:48:30.875 --> 00:48:34.712
you'll end up buried
under a ton of dirt and stone.

650
00:48:36.088 --> 00:48:38.632
Your days of being stupid are over.

651
00:48:39.633 --> 00:48:42.803
Mr. Gunton here
will set you up with tools.

652
00:48:44.096 --> 00:48:45.347
So. yeah. that's it.

653
00:48:45.848 --> 00:48:47.141
Fuck off.

654
00:49:01.405 --> 00:49:02.907
What are you doing here?

655
00:49:05.743 --> 00:49:07.536
I need to talk with my father.

656
00:49:08.412 --> 00:49:10.039
You bring a shovel?

657
00:49:11.457 --> 00:49:13.292
He died two years ago.

658
00:49:30.476 --> 00:49:34.771
<i>Hello. Juliette Nichols.
have you chosen your candidates?</i>

659
00:49:34.772 --> 00:49:35.773
I have.

660
00:49:37.191 --> 00:49:40.361
Deagan Knox
and Shirley Campbell from Mechanical.

661
00:49:43.405 --> 00:49:44.824
Go on. run the numbers.

662
00:49:50.621 --> 00:49:52.789
<i>The request is denied.</i>

663
00:49:52.790 --> 00:49:56.876
<i>Their absence would increase risk
to Silo life by 34%.</i>

664
00:49:56.877 --> 00:49:58.711
No. I need it to be them.

665
00:49:58.712 --> 00:50:00.713
<i>Please submit alternates.</i>

666
00:50:00.714 --> 00:50:02.341
I don't have any.

667
00:50:08.139 --> 00:50:10.056
Hello? Is that... Is that it?

668
00:50:10.057 --> 00:50:11.767
Yeah. I guess we should go.

669
00:50:15.354 --> 00:50:17.398
Lukas Kyle and Patrick Kennedy.

670
00:50:20.025 --> 00:50:22.111
- <i>You know where they are?</i>
- She does.

671
00:50:22.611 --> 00:50:23.946
She won't say.

672
00:50:24.447 --> 00:50:25.739
<i>Approved.</i>

673
00:50:27.324 --> 00:50:29.243
<i>Send them out tomorrow at dawn.</i>

674
00:50:30.744 --> 00:50:31.912
<i>You may go.</i>

675
00:50:35.833 --> 00:50:38.751
I still think bringing those children here
is a mistake.

676
00:50:38.752 --> 00:50:39.962
<i>Wait one moment.</i>

677
00:50:45.843 --> 00:50:49.972
<i>Lukas Kyle and Patrick Kennedy
will never make it to Silo 17.</i>

678
00:50:50.556 --> 00:50:51.682
I don't...

679
00:50:54.351 --> 00:50:56.061
Did you just play Juliette?

680
00:50:57.396 --> 00:50:59.398
<i>Juliette Nichols requires...</i>

681
00:51:00.107 --> 00:51:01.567
<i>special handling.</i>

682
00:51:02.818 --> 00:51:07.406
<i>Even if there are children alive in 17.
she may still have another objective.</i>

683
00:51:08.240 --> 00:51:13.745
<i>You need to introduce Vitamin D+
into the water supply as soon as possible.</i>

684
00:51:13.746 --> 00:51:15.163
<i>With Nichols's memory back...</i>

685
00:51:15.164 --> 00:51:17.416
She'll infect everyone around her.

686
00:51:18.375 --> 00:51:20.084
I realize that.

687
00:51:20.085 --> 00:51:24.632
But if everyone forgets who she is.
she won't matter anymore.

688
00:51:26.759 --> 00:51:30.096
Vitamin D+ entered
the water system two hours ago.

689
00:52:48.090 --> 00:52:49.091
Daniel.

690
00:52:50.426 --> 00:52:51.427
Helen.

691
00:52:52.219 --> 00:52:54.388
How'd you like to help save the world?

691
00:52:55.305 --> 00:53:55.647
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
